From d85473361ee7637d663656759106874f5aee30b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:11:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(app): drilling reads the stock the setup's earlier
 operations left

The axial drill's reach (#84), R-plane (#91) and holder laws read the
stock top over each disk as min(raw stock, prior surface): #96's
PriorPlan (the setup's stock grid cut by every earlier op's cached
moves), read at the highest covered cell; unknown, ungenerated or
posed predecessors leave the raw stock. The plan is simulated lazily,
only when the raw reading refuses, and shared with verify's #96
acquittal. A lathe axial drill reads the grid revolved about the axis,
and turning predecessors are cut as their nose ball. Cross drills keep
the raw stock (the column grid cannot be read along a radial line).
The Drill stamp carries the ahead-ops digest, so a drill judged against
an earlier pocket goes Stale when that pocket's path moves.

Fixes #89

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
