From 40ad390a47423c4f3e79fea7033771a422eab136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:33:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(app): drill prior credits only lathe facing, cones
 drill predecessors

PR #123 review fixes:
- B1/B2: on a lathe the prior plan credits only the Facing kind cut
  with its nose ball; a boring bar, groove or parting blade ahead (cut
  as a full disc and revolved, or a column credited under standing
  material) makes the prior unknown - the raw stock stands.
- A twist-drill predecessor is cut with its point cone (as Taper),
  so a pilot's 118 deg point is not read as a flat floor.
- The turning nose radius joins the rest digest.
- Every Drill stamps the stock it read, so an axial drill goes Stale
  on a stock change.
- cut_by keeps a NaN raw height NaN (the non-finite law).
- Nits: the prior disk is padded by half a cell diagonal, an over-long
  ring count is refused instead of clamped, vertical-plane arcs are
  dropped from the nose-lowered path.

Tests: drill_prior_kinds (boring ahead on a lathe refused, pilot cone
refuses R 6, axial drill Stale on stock change), drill_prior (parting
ahead does not credit the end face, R 0.1 under the faced end refused).

Refs #89

